## Security OS (`.ai.soc/`)

**Lost on security?** `.ai.soc/START_HERE.md` · **Router:** `@soc-director - <what you want>`

### SOC source resolution (thin-client)

SOC_SOURCE=REPLACE_SOCSOURCE

The agent MUST resolve `.ai.soc/` references from `$SOC_SOURCE` (thin-client mode). When `SOC_SOURCE` is set and readable, read `.ai.soc/skills/<id>/skill.md` from `$SOC_SOURCE/skills/<id>/skill.md`. Skills, templates, and scripts resolve from the source at runtime. When `SOC_SOURCE` is missing or unreadable, skills resolve locally from this repo's `.ai.soc/` (fat-client mode).

**Verify deployment:** `bash $SOC_SOURCE/scripts/soc-deploy-basic.sh verify .` — read-only audit of this `.cursorrules` (SOC_SOURCE correctness/reachability, stale skill handles, `.work.soc/` skeleton, sister frameworks). Exit 0 = coherent. Run after any deploy/update or whenever `SOC_SOURCE` moves.

### Framework paths

Sister frameworks live as siblings on disk. Paths below are templated with `{WORK_ROOT}` for portability — no tool-specific config needed.

**`{WORK_ROOT}` resolution (in priority order):**

1. If a `WORK_ROOT:` line exists anywhere above this section, use that absolute path verbatim.
2. Otherwise, infer it as the **parent directory of this repository** (the repo this `.cursorrules` lives in). Sibling frameworks are then `{WORK_ROOT}/<framework>` (list below).
3. If neither resolves an existing sibling directory, stop routing with a one-line `framework not installed here` message — never silently route into the void.

| Framework | Path | Director |
|-----------|------|----------|
| Security OS (`.ai.soc`) | `$SOC_SOURCE` (thin-client source) | `@soc-director` |
| Agent OS (`.ai`) | `{WORK_ROOT}/.ai` | `@ai-director` |
| UI Design OS (`.ai.ui`) | `{WORK_ROOT}/.ai.ui` | `@ui-director` |
| Business OS (`.ai.biz`) | `{WORK_ROOT}/.ai.biz` | `@biz-director` |
| CTO Professor OS (`.ai.cto`) | `{WORK_ROOT}/.ai.cto` | `@cto-director` |
| Flutter Agent OS (`.ai.flutter`) | `{WORK_ROOT}/.ai.flutter` | `@flutter-director` |
| MLT Agent OS (`.ai.mlt`) | `{WORK_ROOT}/.ai.mlt` | `@mlt-director` |

Family naming: sisters may also live as `pilo.ai.<fw>.logicbison` — the shared discovery rule (`$SOC_SOURCE/scripts/sister-discovery.sh`) resolves both forms; family-named sources derive sisters as `<source basename with <fw> inserted before its last .segment>` (`.ai`-prefixed sources resolve `.ai.<fw>` directly).

### Path resolution

x-director and ai-director resolve frameworks from the table above. Substitute `{WORK_ROOT}` per the resolution rules at the top of this section before reading any framework path. Preflight check before routing: verify the framework's `skills/README.md` exists at the declared path. If absent, stop routing with a one-line `framework not installed here` message — never silently route into the void.

