**Sessions:** `@soc-session` — opens and closes SOC sessions

**Reports:** every SOC skill response closes per the Operator handoff contract in `skills/SKILL_DEPENDENCIES.md` (resolved via `$SOC_SOURCE` in thin-client mode) — Form A single line when nothing is needed, otherwise Form B (`**Needs your approval:**` / `**Needs your answer:**` / `**Next step:**`).

### Data Loss Prevention (SOC deploy invariant)

**Permission scope:** Explicit human/operator permission authorizes **only the current request / current case**. It is never standing or permanent. Prior approval does not authorize a later destructive action.

- **Git:** NEVER `git commit` or `git push` unless explicitly requested in the **same message**. NEVER amend, rebase, rewrite history, `reset --hard`, `clean -fd`/`-fdx`, or force-push unless explicitly requested in the **same message**.
- **Files:** NEVER delete/unlink/`rm` files or directories unless explicitly requested in the **same message**. Narrow exception: agent-created ephemeral files under `tmp/` (or designated temp dir) created by this agent in the **current session**.
- **Databases / persistent stores:** NEVER `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, wipe, factory-reset, mass-delete, or run destructive down-migrations; NEVER remove/prune Docker/Podman volumes or data dirs holding persistent state — unless explicitly requested in the **same message**.

